{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|NL.}}, from {{etyl|fr}} {{term|urée|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|οὖρον||urine|sc=Grek}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{biochemistry}} A water-soluble [[organic compound]], CO(NH<sub>2</sub>)<sub>2</sub>, formed by the [[metabolism]] of [[protein]]s and excreted in the [[urine]].
# {{chemistry}} Any ''N''-[[substituted]] [[derivative]] of urea, with the general formula (R<sub>1</sub>R<sub>2</sub>N)CO(NR<sub>3</sub>R<sub>4</sub>).

